DEBUGLEVEL 0
FILE_OPEN 1 0
FILE_READ L# all values have a range of 0 to 10. More is only meaningful for the range variable.
 0
FILE_READ L# the "meta"-meaning of a value was used by me to deduce the AI abilities from the abilities of the real program.
 0
FILE_READ L# 1st column "name": Program name
 0
FILE_READ L# 2nd column "rs": Program reaction speed (meta: program execution speed)
 0
FILE_READ L# 3rd column "er": Reaction in an emergency
 0
FILE_READ L# 4th column "vr": Program viewing range
 0
FILE_READ L# 5th column "trace": wall tracing ability (meta: how good can the program handle texts?)
 0
FILE_READ L# 6th column "close": close combat ability (meta: how good can you control the prog with keyboard alone?)
 0
FILE_READ L# 7th column "path": pathfinding ability  (meta: mouse control quality)
 0
FILE_READ L# 8th column "loop": ability to detect closed areas and to close the enemy in (meta: is the program secure?)
 0
FILE_READ L# 9th column "cycle": ability to evade or cross enemy cycles (meta: is there a feud going on with users of another similar program?)
 0
FILE_READ L#10th column "tunl": ability to avoid dangerous tunnels ( meta: is it stable?)
 0
FILE_READ L#11th column "tr-det": ability to react on enemy cycles tracing the own wall (meta: meaningful error messages)
 0
FILE_READ L#12th column "state": state the AI starts in (0: survive, 1: trace, 2: closecombat, 3: pathfind)
 0
FILE_READ L#13th column "str": time the AI drives straight on at the beginning
 0
FILE_READ L#14th column "sttch": time before the first state change
 0
FILE_READ L# Feel free to modify the AIs or add new ones; but be aware that the interpretation
 0
FILE_READ L# of these values is not yet final. PLEASE DON'T send me your changes. They'll
 0
FILE_READ L# probably be useless when I get them.
 0
FILE_READ L#name		rs  er  vr  trace  close  path  loop  cycle  tunl  tr-det  state  str  sttch
